[Music]  whoa take it easy there Pathfinder you  might be feeling a little dizzy or  lightheaded this is normal for anyone  who just woke up from a 600 year nap  your memory might be a little fuzzy as  well so let me catch you up on our  Andromeda protocol and what you need to  know before you start exploring our new  home if you're a Mass Effect fan make  sure to check out our behind-the-scenes  documentary on Andromeda hit that  subscribe button so you don't miss a  thing  once you've thought out we'll let you  loose to explore yose and other sweet  planets I can't show you right now there  are a few things to keep in mind first  the environment is hostile not only do  you have to deal with creatures like  this  but you also have to worry about weather  and radiation  heõs has a radiation problem if you  wander too far from a safe area or the  nomads you'll get fried based on what  we've played it seems like these  environmental issues clear up as you  progress through the story but there are  some hazards that your Nomad won't even  protect you from access issues equipment  nearby speaking of your Nomad it's your  trusty 6 wheel steed no you can't  whistle it over to you like a horse if  you lose it but you can fast travel to a  drop pod and call it in the planets  you'll be exploring are huge so it's in  your best interest not to stray too far  from your vehicle if you're having  trouble getting up an incline you can  activate six wheel drive this will slow  you down but it's the best and only way  to get this hunk of metal up a hill and  never forget if you're in a hurry to get  back to the tempest you can hold down Y  triangle or tea and you'll load right  back into your ship ascent just go  leaving Apple all clear as a pathfinder  you're expected to do some research as  well don't worry you won't be tested on  the various biomes of es but a good  Pathfinder is responsible for scanning  and cataloguing technology vegetation  and wildlife everything you scan will  net you research points for one of three  different categories Helius cluster  Milky Way and remnant you can then use  your research points of the Rd terminal  on the tempest to craft weapon and armor  blueprints once a blueprint has been  created you can Forge that item using  minerals and other resources you've  salvaged from scanning planets breaking  down weapons and armor mining with the  nomads and just good old-fashioned  picking stuff up if you think science is  dumb you can also buy weapons from  vendors but you'll be doing more than  just driving around in scanning planets  Andromeda's combat has undergone some  significant changes and the result is a  much more liberating experience  abilities can be combined in combo'd off  of each other more easily and the  jetpack adds a lot more verticality to  the battles  unfortunately the tactical commands from  the original trilogy are gone you can  still tell your squad to go here or  regroup but you can't access their  powers this means the experimentation is  largely up to you there are three  different types of abilities tech combat  and biotic personally I stick with  biotic abilities but I wouldn't ignore  tech or combat if you like to carry more  than two guns at a time invest in the  combat Fitness skill tree a basic biotic  combo is pull and throw hold down your  pull ability and once you've pulled them  up close use throw and you'll send them  off to the next Galaxy  keep in mind you can only have three  abilities mapped at a time but Andromeda  does have something called favorites  once you've assigned three powers you  like together you can favorite it now  hold the weapon select button and you  can swap between different power sets  this may not be super useful early on  but later it comes in handy and remember  if you aren't happy with the abilities  you've invested in you can always head  on over to the medical Bay in the  tempest where you can respect for a  small fee but with powers like these why  would you Andromeda also introduces a  contextual cover system to be honest  it's not great but make sure you know  how to swap shoulders while and cover  otherwise you're gonna have a bad time  luckily though movement and verticality  plays a much bigger role the recharge  time for your jump and dash are very  short so it's in your best interest to  keep moving and if you aim while in the  air you can hover and take shots at your  enemies from above even with all this  fancy movement though don't ignore cover  altogether your shield will regenerate  faster if you're hunkered down  congratulations Pathfinder you're ready  to explore the next frontier as you  research and trailblaze the Helius  cluster you'll learn a lot more tips and  tricks  leave those findings and discoveries in  the comments below to help out your  fellow pathfinders for more on Mass  Effect Andromeda make sure to subscribe  and as always thanks for watching

